WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.200
SmartVest Investing Academy.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:06.400
Lesson 7: What is Compounding?

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:13.725
Why is compounding often described as the most powerful mathematical force in personal wealth creation?

4
00:00:13.725 --> 00:00:18.525
Simple interest earns returns only on your original principal.

5
00:00:18.525 --> 00:00:27.275
Compounding, however, means earning returns on your original principal PLUS all the accumulated returns from previous years.

6
00:00:27.275 --> 00:00:31.487
Think of a snowball rolling down a long snowy mountain.

7
00:00:31.488 --> 00:00:35.962
At first, it gathers only a tiny amount of snow.

8
00:00:35.962 --> 00:00:44.462
But as it rolls further, its enlarged surface area picks up massive amounts of new snow with every single revolution.

9
00:00:44.462 --> 00:00:47.987
That mathematical momentum is compounding.

10
00:00:47.987 --> 00:00:51.425
Let us look at a hypothetical example.

11
00:00:51.425 --> 00:00:57.637
Suppose you invest ₹1,00,000 at a hypothetical annual return of 10%.

12
00:00:57.638 --> 00:01:04.388
In Year 1, you earn ₹10,000, bringing your total to ₹1,10,000.

13
00:01:04.388 --> 00:01:14.938
In Year 2, you earn 10% not on your initial ₹1 Lakh, but on ₹1,10,000—giving you ₹11,000 in gains.

14
00:01:14.938 --> 00:01:24.112
By Year 10, without adding any new money, your ₹1 Lakh grows to approximately ₹2.59 Lakhs.

15
00:01:24.112 --> 00:01:29.062
By Year 20, it reaches ₹6.72 Lakhs.

16
00:01:29.062 --> 00:01:34.875
And by Year 30, it surges past ₹17.44 Lakhs!

17
00:01:34.875 --> 00:01:42.888
Over 90% of your ultimate wealth was created purely by returns generating their own returns in the final decade.

18
00:01:42.888 --> 00:01:50.112
Many beginners assume that to benefit from compounding, you must start with a huge amount of capital.

19
00:01:50.112 --> 00:01:52.800
That is completely false.

20
00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:57.513
The most critical variable in the compounding formula is TIME.

21
00:01:57.513 --> 00:02:07.925
An investor who starts with ₹2,000 a month in their twenties often accumulates more wealth than someone starting with ₹10,000 a month in their forties.

22
00:02:07.925 --> 00:02:13.363
Remember that compounding requires patience and uninterrupted consistency.

23
00:02:13.363 --> 00:02:19.538
Frequent withdrawals or panic-selling during market dips breaks the compounding chain.

24
00:02:19.537 --> 00:02:29.162
Compounding is financial momentum where returns generate returns; starting early and giving time to your investments is the true secret of wealth.

25
00:02:29.162 --> 00:02:32.213
